{
  "file": "common childhood",
  "page": 78,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        113.12979888916016,
        27.289522171020508,
        340.4130554199219,
        35.34652328491211
      ],
      "text": "RECOMMENDATIONS FOR MANAGEMENT OF COMMON CHILDHOOD CONDITIONS",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 7.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        59.74208068847656,
        399.0828552246094,
        73.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "antibiotics (i.e. chloramphenicol, ampicillin, amoxicillin) or cephalosporins (i.e.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        72.74208068847656,
        399.07281494140625,
        86.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "cefixime, ceftriaxone) in children. However, there is a general trend in favour of using",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        85.74208068847656,
        399.1128845214844,
        99.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "fluoroquinolones as first line treatment, and either 3rd generation cephalosporins",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        98.74208068847656,
        399.09283447265625,
        112.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "or azithromycin as second line antibiotics for enteric fever due to the rising level of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        111.74208068847656,
        208.80294799804688,
        125.2320785522461
      ],
      "text": "resistance in many parts of the world.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        124.74208068847656,
        399.1015625,
        138.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "In children, there was a high proportion of nalidixic acid-resistant strains; older",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        137.74208068847656,
        399.0627746582031,
        151.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "fluoroquinolones increased clinical failures compared with azithromycin (OR 2.67,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        150.74208068847656,
        399.11285400390625,
        164.23208618164062
      ],
      "text": "95% CI 1.16 to 6.11; 125 participants, one trial), with no differences using newer",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        163.7421112060547,
        399.09295654296875,
        177.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "fluoroquinolones (285 participants, one trial). Fluoroquinolones and cefixime were",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        176.7421112060547,
        399.0629577636719,
        190.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "not statistically significantly different (82 participants, one trial).Trials comparing",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        189.7421112060547,
        399.1129150390625,
        203.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "different durations of fluoroquinolone treatment also were not statistically",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        202.7421112060547,
        399.06298828125,
        216.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "significantly different (889 participants, nine trials). Norfloxacin had more clinical",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        215.7421112060547,
        320.6730041503906,
        229.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "failures than other fluoroquinolones (417 participants, five trials).",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        228.7421112060547,
        287.85150146484375,
        242.23211669921875
      ],
      "text": "Indirect evidence from the adults showed that there is:",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.54180145263672,
        247.41151428222656,
        399.0519104003906,
        260.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "Moderate quality evidence that fluoroquinolones are superior to chloramphenicol",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        249.63796997070312,
        63.541900634765625,
        258.6379699707031
      ],
      "text": "n",
      "font": "ZapfDingbats",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        268.17138671875,
        260.1915283203125,
        365.8612976074219,
        273.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "see GRADE table A7.24",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        260.4114990234375,
        371.0462951660156,
        273.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "in reducing relapse and duration of hospital stay ( ).",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.54180145263672,
        273.4114990234375,
        399.0618591308594,
        286.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "Low quality evidence that fluoroquinolones are superior to amoxicillin or",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        275.6379699707031,
        63.541900634765625,
        284.6379699707031
      ],
      "text": "n",
      "font": "ZapfDingbats",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        320.0111999511719,
        286.1915283203125,
        399.05108642578125,
        299.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "see GRADE table",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        286.4114990234375,
        320.4814147949219,
        299.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "ampicillin in reducing clinical or microbiological failure (",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        299.1915283203125,
        91.74150848388672,
        312.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": "A7.25",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        91.4302978515625,
        299.4114990234375,
        96.94029998779297,
        312.9015197753906
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.54180145263672,
        312.411376953125,
        399.12176513671875,
        325.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "Low quality evidence that fluoroquinolones are superior to ceftriaxone in reducing",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        314.6378479003906,
        63.541900634765625,
        323.6378479003906
      ],
      "text": "n",
      "font": "ZapfDingbats",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        321.1441955566406,
        325.19140625,
        399.04412841796875,
        338.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "see GRADE table",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        325.411376953125,
        321.6215515136719,
        338.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "clinical failure in settings of low nalidixic acid resistance (",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        338.19140625,
        91.74150848388672,
        351.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "A7.25",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        91.4302978515625,
        338.411376953125,
        96.94029998779297,
        351.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        63.54180145263672,
        351.411376953125,
        399.061767578125,
        364.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "Moderate quality evidence that azithromycin is superior to fluoroquinolones in",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        353.6378479003906,
        63.541900634765625,
        362.6378479003906
      ],
      "text": "n",
      "font": "ZapfDingbats",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        347.6506042480469,
        364.19140625,
        399.050537109375,
        377.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "see GRADE",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        364.411376953125,
        348.1214599609375,
        377.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "reducing clinical failures in settings of high nalidixic acid resistance (",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        377.19140625,
        114.1915054321289,
        390.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": "table A7.26",
      "font": "MinionPro-Semibold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        114.00299835205078,
        377.411376953125,
        119.51300048828125,
        390.9013977050781
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        396.0806884765625,
        399.1228942871094,
        409.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "There was a wide range of different durations of therapy compared in several trials,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        409.0806884765625,
        399.0228576660156,
        422.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "and the trials for each comparison were small – mostly with small sample sizes",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        422.0806884765625,
        399.1127624511719,
        435.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "and lacking considerably in statistical power. The review found only two trials that",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        435.0806884765625,
        399.11279296875,
        448.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "compared a short-course regimen (7 days or less) with a long-course regimen (more",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        448.0806884765625,
        399.0827331542969,
        461.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "than 7 days). Clinical failure, microbiological failure, and relapse rates were low in",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        461.0806884765625,
        327.0530090332031,
        474.5707092285156
      ],
      "text": "both arms, but the data were not sufficient to make any conclusion.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        485.59930419921875,
        163.95286560058594,
        497.58929443359375
      ],
      "text": "8.6.2\t Benefits and risks",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        501.2439270019531,
        88.77290344238281,
        513.3839111328125
      ],
      "text": "Benefits",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Obli",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        514.25390625,
        399.1327209472656,
        527.743896484375
      ],
      "text": "Although there was no difference in the clinical failure in patients without MDR",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        527.25390625,
        399.0829772949219,
        540.743896484375
      ],
      "text": "when fluoroquinolones are compared with first line antibiotics, there was a clear",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        540.25390625,
        399.0729675292969,
        553.743896484375
      ],
      "text": "benefit in favour of fluoroquinolones in fever clearance, microbiological failure, and",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        553.25390625,
        399.03302001953125,
        566.743896484375
      ],
      "text": "relapse. There is also a clear benefit of using fluoroquinolones over chloramphenicol;",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        566.2539672851562,
        399.10272216796875,
        579.7439575195312
      ],
      "text": "reduced relapse rate and convalescent faecal carriage (298 patients in three studies",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        579.2539672851562,
        399.07281494140625,
        592.7439575195312
      ],
      "text": "with RR 0.17, 95% CI 0.04 to 0.70); and reduced risk of treatment failure given",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        592.2539672851562,
        250.552978515625,
        605.7439575195312
      ],
      "text": "increasing frequency of participants with MDR.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        222.3542938232422,
        644.9403076171875,
        230.68829345703125,
        655.2992553710938
      ],
      "text": "64",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}